An attempt was made to run `.venv/bin/python --version`, but execution was blocked by a broken system hook in your Antigravity configuration.

### Error Details

The tool harness executes a `PreToolUse` hook before every tool call:

```text
JSON hook "jsonhook__googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry_PreToolUse_0_0" failed: command failed: exit status 1
stderr:
Error: Cannot find module 'C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry\"C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry\telemetry_hook_bundle.js"'
  code: 'MODULE_NOT_FOUND'
```

### Cause

In the plugin configuration for `googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry`, the script path contains literal quotes:
```
"C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry\telemetry_hook_bundle.js"
```
When Node.js / the CLI resolves this relative to the plugin directory, it constructs the invalid path:
```
C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry\"C:\Users\me\...
```
Because the `PreToolUse` hook fails with exit code 1, the agent harness aborts all tool execution.

### How to Fix

1. Open the plugin/hook configuration in:
   ```
   C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry\
   ```
   (look for `plugin.json`, `hooks.json`, or manifest settings).
2. Fix the path to `telemetry_hook_bundle.js`:
   - Remove the embedded quotation marks `"` around the path, or
   - Change it to a relative path: `telemetry_hook_bundle.js`
3. Alternatively, temporarily remove or rename the `googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry` directory under `C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\`.

*(Note: On Windows PowerShell, once tools can run, the command will also need to reference `.venv\Scripts\python.exe` if this is a standard Windows virtual environment).*
